      "problem": "Suppose $n=-10-30q,$ where $q\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is even.",
      "worked_solution": "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is even since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =-10-30q \\\\  & =2({{-5-15q}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=-5-15q,$ which is an integer.",
